{ Tests for the generated codecs of the consumer-group APIs (phase K2's
  foundation) against the captures of Kafka.TestCaptures
  (docs/codec-captures.md): FindCoordinator v0-v6, OffsetCommit v2-v10,
  OffsetFetch v1-v10, ConsumerGroupHeartbeat v0-v1 and ConsumerGroupDescribe
  v0-v1, built by hand and accepted by a Kafka 4.4.0 broker, and the Java
  client 4.4.0 in a KIP-848 group.

  - Every hand-built request, rebuilt from the generated records, encodes to
    the captured bytes (the topic id, which the broker chose, is read from
    the capture).
  - The broker's answers decode to what was asked: the coordinator (node 1,
    localhost:9092) in the v0-v3 fields and in v4's list; every commit
    accepted; every OffsetFetch version reads the last commit (110, "commit
    v10"); a member joining gets its id back, an epoch, the heartbeat
    interval and an assignment of the subscribed topic's partitions;
    ConsumerGroupDescribe sees it Stable with the uniform assignor; leaving
    gives epoch -1.
  - The nullable struct (ConsumerGroupHeartbeatResponse.Assignment, the
    generator's first): Java's first heartbeat, answered NOT_COORDINATOR
    by a broker that had just started, has none; the one that joined has one; a null
    and a present one each encode back to the same bytes, and Init makes it
    null.

  DUnitX master: the FPCUnit mirror in tests/Unit/fpc is generated by
  tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py. }

